<thead>
<tr>
<th>Nutrient Component</th>
<th>Concentration</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>
<div><b>Glomus aggregatum</b></div></td>
<td class="percentage">5,500 viable propagules per gram (0.36 US oz)</td>
<td>Promotes vigorous root branching and enhances the uptake of phosphorus, zinc, and copper, thereby aiding early plant establishment.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div><b>Glomus etunicatum</b></div></td>
<td class="percentage">5,500 viable propagules per gram (0.36 US oz)</td>
<td>Enhances drought tolerance and improves nutrient access in sandy or low-fertility soils.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div><b>Glomus geosporum</b></div></td>
<td class="percentage">5,500 viable propagules per gram (0.36 US oz)</td>
<td>Supports growth in cooler or wetter soils, improving plant resilience under stress.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div><b>Glomus intraradices</b></div></td>
<td class="percentage">5,500 viable propagules per gram (0.36 US oz)</td>
<td>Rapidly colonizes roots, increasing the efficiency of nutrient and water absorption.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div><b>Glomus mosseae</b></div></td>
<td class="percentage">2,000 viable propagules per gram (0.36 US oz)</td>
<td>Provides strong, long-lasting colonization and improved resistance to soil-borne diseases.</td>
